  stripes:
    edges: 2-4 of the 4 edges are solid color bands, each 2-4 cells thick [observed 2-4]; each distinct color; none equal to bg/8/9
    internal: 0 or 1 internal stripe (horizontal OR vertical), 2 cells thick, distinct non-bg/8/9 color different from all edges
    stripe_colors_total: 3-4 distinct colors across all edges+internal
  regions:
    count: 1 (no internal stripe) or 2 (one internal stripe partitions inner rectangle)
    min_size: each region >=5x5, typically >=10 in each dim
    boundaries: each region is bordered on 3-4 sides by stripes (edges and/or the internal stripe); each bounding stripe has a distinct color
  stations (dst):
    definition: 8-connected clusters of color-9 cells NOT adjacent (8-neighborhood) to any 8
    count: equal to number of trains (2-3)
    sizes: distinct per example, drawn from {1, 2, 4} [observed] (1x1 dot, 1x2 line, 2x2 block)
    placement: each station lies strictly inside some region, with >=2 cells of clearance from all stripe boundaries
  trains (src):
    count: 2-3; equals station count
    body_color: 8 (8-connected, forms an irregular blob); 5-20 color-8 cells per train
    bbox: 4-9 rows x 3-8 cols
    couplers (attached 9s): for each train, a unique count in {1,2,4} matching exactly one station's size; couplers are color-9 pixels 8-adjacent to the train's 8-body and NOT forming a station (i.e., touching the 8s)
    coupler_shape: the set of coupler-9 cells, viewed as a sub-sprite attached to the train body, must be congruent (via flip/rotation) to the target station shape so they coincide after the docking transform
    markers: 2-3 non-bg pixels on the train bbox colored with stripe colors; each marker color equals a boundary-stripe color of the TARGET region; markers are positioned so that, relative to the coupler centroid, each marker lies toward the side where its matching boundary stripe sits (this uniquely determines rotation/flip)
    placement: trains live anywhere inside any region (can be in a different region than their target station); do not overlap stripes; no two trains overlap
  transform (input -> output):
    - erase each train from its original location (fill with bg; do not erase the station 9s)
    - for each train, apply the unique flip/rotation that aligns its markers with the target region's stripe-color directions
    - translate so its coupler-9s land exactly on the target station's 9 cells
    - redraw all non-bg, non-9 pixels of the transformed train at the new position; station 9s remain as-is (couplers are thus absorbed into station cells)
  invariants:
    - count(8) preserved between input and output
    - count(9) halved: couplers removed, stations remain
    - stripes, bg, region geometry unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (assembled docked state), then undock and scatter trains back into the grid
  steps:
    - 1. pick grid H,W (13-30 x 16-28), bg color, and 2-4 edge stripe positions (each 2-4 thick) with distinct non-bg/8/9 colors
