  92:     """
  93:     Rotate each 2x2 block's four diagonal corner colors clockwise, then extend the rotated colors outward as diagonal rays.
  94: 
  95:     Input structure
  96:     - The background is the dominant color.
  97:     - One foreground color forms one or more solid 2x2 blocks.
  98:     - Each block has four non-background, non-block corner pixels diagonally adjacent to it.
  99: 
 100:     Rule
 101:     - Around every block, move the NW corner color to NE, NE to SE, SE to SW, and SW to NW.
 102:     - From each rotated corner, paint along the outward diagonal until the grid edge or another 2x2 block is reached.
 103:     - If a ray reaches a same-colored outgoing corner of another block that has its own visible continuation, stop the incoming ray at that junction.
 104: 
 105:     Key insight
 106:     - The 2x2 blocks are color rotators and ray blockers; the corner pixels are not independent dots but the four ports of each block.
 107:     """
 108:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
 109:     assert g.ndim == 2
 110:     bg = int(get_bg(g))
 111:     block_color = _block_color(g, bg)
 112: 
 113:     rays: list[Ray] = []
 114:     h, w = g.shape
